WEBVTT

1
00:00:26.041 --> 00:00:30.250


2
00:00:30.250 --> 00:00:32.625
<b>In the previous verse, Lord Krishna explained</b>

3
00:00:32.625 --> 00:00:38.250
<b>how many people in the past were purified </b>
<b>through the penance of spiritual knowledge</b>

4
00:00:38.250 --> 00:00:42.250
<b>and ultimately attained Him.</b>

5
00:00:42.250 --> 00:00:47.500
<b>Attaining Lord Krishna in this way is the </b>
<b>supreme level of spirituality.</b>

6
00:00:47.500 --> 00:00:48.291
<b>However,</b>

7
00:00:48.291 --> 00:00:50.708
<b>there are many people in this universe,</b>

8
00:00:50.708 --> 00:00:54.166
<b>and they are all at different levels of spirituality.</b>

9
00:00:54.166 --> 00:00:59.208
<b>Does Krishna bestow His grace only upon </b>
<b>those who believe in spirituality?</b>

10
00:00:59.208 --> 00:01:02.500
<b>It's possible that someone may </b>
<b>be far from spirituality,</b>

11
00:01:02.500 --> 00:01:06.375
<b>or may not know the joy of attaining Krishna,</b>

12
00:01:06.375 --> 00:01:09.166
<b>and yet Krishna is the Lord of the entire universe.</b>

13
00:01:09.166 --> 00:01:13.875
<b>So, does He not have something </b>
<b>to offer to everyone else?</b>

14
00:01:13.875 --> 00:01:16.875
<b>This verse is the answer to that question.</b>

15
00:01:21.625 --> 00:01:23.833
<b>Lord Krishna says to Arjun,</b>

16
00:01:23.833 --> 00:01:25.166
<b>"O Parth,</b>

17
00:01:25.166 --> 00:01:28.625
<b>in whatever way a person takes refuge in Me,</b>

18
00:01:28.625 --> 00:01:31.791
<b>I reward them accordingly."</b>

19
00:01:31.791 --> 00:01:37.916
<b>In other words, everyone </b>
<b>receives what they seek.</b>

20
00:01:37.916 --> 00:01:41.708
<b>Some devotees love Krishna as their son,</b>

21
00:01:41.708 --> 00:01:44.916
<b>so Krishna appears to them as their son.</b>

22
00:01:44.916 --> 00:01:50.333
<b>Some devotees consider Him their friend, </b>
<b>so Krishna appears as a friend.</b>

23
00:01:50.333 --> 00:01:53.958
<b>Some people, like Kansa, saw Him as an enemy,</b>

24
00:01:53.958 --> 00:01:57.041
<b>so Krishna treated them accordingly.</b>

25
00:01:57.041 --> 00:02:01.333
<b>As your attitude is towards Him, so is His form.</b>

26
00:02:01.333 --> 00:02:03.708
<b>Look at it this way:</b>

27
00:02:03.708 --> 00:02:09.333
<b>when you go to the market, there</b>
<b>are many items available.</b>

28
00:02:09.333 --> 00:02:10.458
<b>But</b>

29
00:02:10.458 --> 00:02:12.666
<b>what do you bring back?</b>

30
00:02:12.666 --> 00:02:15.500
<b>Only what you wanted, right?</b>

31
00:02:15.500 --> 00:02:19.250
<b>Now consider this: Lord Krishna </b>
<b>is the master of this entire world.</b>

32
00:02:19.250 --> 00:02:21.041
<b>He has everything,</b>

33
00:02:21.041 --> 00:02:27.000
<b>but He bestows upon you only according </b>
<b>to your desire and your devotion.</b>

34
00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:30.333
<b>Here, another notion is clarified.</b>

35
00:02:30.333 --> 00:02:32.750
<b>Many people form the notion that</b>

36
00:02:32.750 --> 00:02:39.375
<b>all people following the path of Lord Krishna </b>
<b>reach the same destination, the same goal.</b>

37
00:02:39.375 --> 00:02:41.125
<b>But that is not the case.</b>

38
00:02:41.125 --> 00:02:43.625
<b>Everyone is moving towards Krishna,</b>

39
00:02:43.625 --> 00:02:48.166
<b>but they receive what they desired.</b>

40
00:02:48.166 --> 00:02:51.583
<b>Understand it like this: you are on a train,</b>

41
00:02:51.583 --> 00:02:54.250
<b>and everyone is going in the same direction,</b>

42
00:02:54.250 --> 00:03:00.708
<b>but each person will get off at different </b>
<b>destinations according to their own needs.</b>

43
00:03:00.708 --> 00:03:04.250
<b>This verse also demonstrates </b>
<b>Krishna's generosity.</b>

44
00:03:04.250 --> 00:03:07.750
<b>He inspires everyone to come to Him;</b>

45
00:03:07.750 --> 00:03:10.000
<b>He accepts everyone.</b>

46
00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:17.666
<b>It's not that He rejects those who have </b>
<b>not reached a high level of spirituality.</b>

47
00:03:17.666 --> 00:03:24.625
<b>Krishna is always ready to help </b>
<b>and guide each and every one.</b>

48
00:03:33.333 --> 00:03:38.166
<b>What you desire, you shall receive.</b>

49
00:03:38.166 --> 00:03:47.125
<b>This world, this universe, always responds</b>
<b>to your wishes and your actions.</b>

50
00:03:47.125 --> 00:03:52.250
<b>As your desire, so shall be the fruit.</b>

51
00:03:52.250 --> 00:03:55.333
<b>Fully understand this concept.</b>

52
00:03:55.333 --> 00:04:00.958
<b>And know the difference </b>
<b>between desire and greed.</b>

53
00:04:00.958 --> 00:04:02.541
<b>Think about it,</b>

54
00:04:02.541 --> 00:04:12.750
<b>if a student starts wishing to get the highest </b>
<b>marks in the exam without putting in any effort,</b>

55
00:04:12.750 --> 00:04:16.500
<b>would you call it a desire or greed?</b>

56
00:04:16.500 --> 00:04:22.583
<b>Moreover, if that student is</b>
<b>given the highest marks,</b>

57
00:04:22.583 --> 00:04:27.875
<b>wouldn't it be unfair to the </b>
<b>hardworking students?</b>

58
00:04:27.875 --> 00:04:32.291
<b>Because they too had the same desire, right?</b>

59
00:04:32.291 --> 00:04:35.833
<b>So, know the difference between desire and greed.</b>

60
00:04:35.833 --> 00:04:44.583
<b>The truer one's desire, the greater their </b>
<b>effort, and the results will be accordingly.</b>

61
00:04:44.583 --> 00:04:49.375
<b>Now, someone might become</b>
<b>negative after hearing this.</b>

62
00:04:49.375 --> 00:04:53.875
<b>So think, what are you asking for?</b>

63
00:04:53.875 --> 00:04:59.708
<b>Your words may be anything, </b>
<b> but your mind is negative.</b>

64
00:04:59.708 --> 00:05:06.125
<b>Then, naturally, the response you </b>
<b>get will also be negative, right?</b>

65
00:05:06.125 --> 00:05:13.666
<b>On the other hand, those who display </b>
<b>positivity ultimately receive positivity.</b>

66
00:05:13.666 --> 00:05:19.458
<b>In life, you will attract what you emit.</b>

67
00:05:19.458 --> 00:05:27.083
<b>If in your daily routine, you emit </b>
<b>negativity, doubt, hatred towards others,</b>

68
00:05:27.083 --> 00:05:30.791
<b>then you will receive the same in return, right?</b>

69
00:05:30.791 --> 00:05:37.041
<b>However, if you radiate </b>
<b>positivity, love, and enthusiasm,</b>

70
00:05:37.041 --> 00:05:42.500
<b>you will receive love and positive results in return.</b>

71
00:05:42.500 --> 00:05:44.458
<b>Desire.</b>

72
00:05:44.458 --> 00:05:47.958
<b>Understand this word carefully here.</b>

73
00:05:47.958 --> 00:05:51.708
<b>Desires don't just mean expressing something;</b>

74
00:05:51.708 --> 00:05:58.791
<b>it also means sincerely considering </b>
<b>yourself worthy of that thing.</b>

75
00:05:58.791 --> 00:06:04.041
<b>For example, if you want to win a game,</b>

76
00:06:04.041 --> 00:06:10.291
<b>will you win just by saying </b>
<b>it without putting in the effort?</b>

77
00:06:10.291 --> 00:06:16.833
<b>Do you truly consider yourself </b>
<b>worthy of such a win?</b>

78
00:06:16.833 --> 00:06:22.708
<b>You also know who should be worthy of winning –</b>

79
00:06:22.708 --> 00:06:26.083
<b>the one who prepares, who doesn't accept defeat.</b>

80
00:06:26.083 --> 00:06:33.541
<b>So, if your desire to win is true, you will consider yourself worthy of that victory.</b>

81
00:06:33.541 --> 00:06:41.958
<b>With this belief in your worthiness, you will</b>
<b>put in the effort, prepare, and ultimately win.</b>

82
00:06:41.958 --> 00:06:46.708
<b>And even if you don't win the </b>
<b>first time, you won't be disheartened;</b>

83
00:06:46.708 --> 00:06:51.666
<b>you will work in new ways to </b>
<b>increase your worthiness.</b>

84
00:06:51.666 --> 00:06:53.750
<b>Understand this perspective.</b>

85
00:06:53.750 --> 00:07:00.708
<b>Don't just express your desires; sincerely </b>
<b>believe yourself to be worthy of them.</b>

86
00:07:00.708 --> 00:07:06.666
<b>Then, automatically, you will put in the effort,</b>
<b>positivity will come,</b>

87
00:07:06.666 --> 00:07:11.750
<b>and no obstacle will be able to stop you.</b>

88
00:07:11.750 --> 00:07:14.875
<b>So, especially remember</b>

89
00:07:14.875 --> 00:07:19.041
<b>to engage your mindset only in good things –</b>

90
00:07:19.041 --> 00:07:23.583
<b>hard work, worthiness, honesty, faith.</b>

91
00:07:23.583 --> 00:07:28.750
<b>As you ask of me, so shall I respond.</b>

92
00:07:28.750 --> 00:07:32.458
<b>Understand the full essence of this,</b>

93
00:07:32.458 --> 00:07:38.000
<b>not just the words.</b>

94
00:07:38.000 --> 00:07:47.000
<b>Oh I’m sorry.</b>
<b>Your wish is my command.</b>

95
00:07:51.375 --> 00:07:59.333
<b>In whatever way a person takes refuge in Me,</b>
<b>I reward them accordingly.</b>

96
00:07:59.333 --> 00:08:05.458
<b>Now, it's up to you with what</b>
<b>attitude you come to Me.</b>

97
00:08:05.458 --> 00:08:10.750
<b>If you think about it, this applies </b>
<b>not only in relation to Me</b>

98
00:08:10.750 --> 00:08:16.000
<b>but also in your familial and social contexts.</b>

99
00:08:16.000 --> 00:08:20.750
<b>The attitude you display, the same </b>
<b>response you will receive.</b>

100
00:08:20.750 --> 00:08:25.500
<b> What you want to see, that's what you will see.</b>

101
00:08:25.500 --> 00:08:32.083
<b>For example, the elders in the family have </b>
<b>years of experience and boundless love for you.</b>

102
00:08:32.083 --> 00:08:38.125
<b>If you approach them with this attitude,</b>

103
00:08:38.125 --> 00:08:43.916
<b>you will see the love in their words and gain </b>
<b>numerous experiences worth learning from.</b>

104
00:08:43.916 --> 00:08:52.208
<b>On the other hand, some people start seeing </b>
<b>the elders in the family as a burden, </b>

105
00:08:52.208 --> 00:08:55.708
<b>so then they only see the burden.</b>

106
00:08:55.708 --> 00:08:58.750
<b>Think about it, unfortunately,</b>

107
00:08:58.750 --> 00:09:00.791
<b>these people are deprived</b>

108
00:09:00.791 --> 00:09:06.791
<b>of such a huge treasure of experience and </b>
<b>love standing right in front of them,</b>

109
00:09:06.791 --> 00:09:11.833
<b>simply because their eyes were closed to all of it.</b>

110
00:09:11.833 --> 00:09:15.958
<b>Similarly, when there's a disagreement </b>
<b>with someone in the family,</b>

111
00:09:15.958 --> 00:09:20.916
<b>if you look for faults, the other </b>
<b>person will be at fault.</b>

112
00:09:20.916 --> 00:09:29.125
<b>But if you want to see a resolution to that </b>
<b>disagreement, you will find that too.</b>

113
00:09:29.125 --> 00:09:33.458
<b>Now think, what was your desire?</b>

114
00:09:33.458 --> 00:09:37.166
<b>Society and family are like a mirror.</b>

115
00:09:37.166 --> 00:09:42.416
<b>If you give respect, cooperation, love to others,</b>

116
00:09:42.416 --> 00:09:48.208
<b>these same things will be reflected </b>
<b>back to you from this mirror.</b>

117
00:09:48.208 --> 00:09:55.833
<b>Think about it, in the family, in society, </b>
<b>what are you seeing? What are you looking for?</b>

118
00:09:55.833 --> 00:09:58.000
<b> That's what you are going to get.</b>

119
00:09:58.000 --> 00:10:02.291
<b>And if that's the case, look for the good things,</b>

120
00:10:02.291 --> 00:10:07.041
<b>seek them out. </b>
<b>Understand this concept.</b>

121
00:10:07.041 --> 00:10:09.208
<b>There’s a lot of depth in it.</b>

122
00:10:09.208 --> 00:10:12.875
<b>And anyway, I am here always with you.</b>

123
00:10:17.500 --> 00:10:24.833
<b>As your attitude will be, as your faith will be, </b>
<b>and as your actions will be,</b>

124
00:10:24.833 --> 00:10:28.208
<b>accordingly you will receive the results.</b>

125
00:10:28.208 --> 00:10:34.541
<b>Think about it, you are sitting at home, </b>
<b>and a cool breeze is blowing outside.</b>

126
00:10:34.541 --> 00:10:37.666
<b>Now, the more you open the </b>
<b>windows of the house,</b>

127
00:10:37.666 --> 00:10:41.166
<b>the more the breeze will be </b>
<b>able to come inside, right?</b>

128
00:10:41.166 --> 00:10:44.125
<b>If you shut the window completely,</b>

129
00:10:44.125 --> 00:10:49.000
<b>will that breeze be able to enter </b>
<b>the house then? No, right?</b>

130
00:10:49.000 --> 00:10:53.666
<b>So, if you don't have the </b>
<b>desire to absorb something,</b>

131
00:10:53.666 --> 00:10:58.333
<b>then how will that thing benefit you?</b>

132
00:10:58.333 --> 00:11:01.958
<b>This concept is absolutely applicable in </b>
<b>the professional environment as well.</b>

133
00:11:01.958 --> 00:11:06.583
<b>In the professional environment, </b>
<b>you encounter many experienced people.</b>

134
00:11:06.583 --> 00:11:09.791
<b>Some become your mentors.</b>

135
00:11:09.791 --> 00:11:15.208
<b>But how much of their guidance </b>
<b>you will be able to absorb</b>

136
00:11:15.208 --> 00:11:24.541
<b>depends on how much you have kept the </b>
<b>windows of your mind and heart open to learn.</b>

137
00:11:24.541 --> 00:11:30.500
<b>If you start believing that you</b>
<b>already know everything,</b>

138
00:11:30.500 --> 00:11:37.458
<b>then indirectly your desire is that </b>
<b>you don't want to learn anything new.</b>

139
00:11:37.458 --> 00:11:39.958
<b>And that's exactly what will happen.</b>

140
00:11:39.958 --> 00:11:47.208
<b>Even with good mentors around, </b>
<b>you won't be able to learn anything new. </b>

141
00:11:47.208 --> 00:11:51.291
<b>But on the other hand, if you have </b>
<b>an intense desire to learn,</b>

142
00:11:51.291 --> 00:11:55.541
<b>then the windows of your mind </b>
<b>and heart will remain open,</b>

143
00:11:55.541 --> 00:12:04.083
<b>your nature will remain humble, and </b>
<b>as a result, a mentor will be able to teach you a lot.</b>

144
00:12:04.083 --> 00:12:08.833
<b>Therefore, in the professional environment, </b>
<b>always remain humble,</b>

145
00:12:08.833 --> 00:12:13.166
<b>respect everyone, keep an openness to new ideas.</b>

146
00:12:13.166 --> 00:12:16.166
<b>This will determine your progress.</b>

147
00:12:16.166 --> 00:12:18.833
<b>Actually, a learner can gain</b>

148
00:12:18.833 --> 00:12:26.916
<b>some learning from children, from the leaves </b>
<b>of trees, from every living thing in this universe.</b>

149
00:12:26.916 --> 00:12:29.458
<b>In the professional environment, you have </b>

150
00:12:29.458 --> 00:12:35.500
<b>a treasure of numerous experienced individuals </b>
<b>and numerous collaborators around you.</b>

151
00:12:35.500 --> 00:12:37.958
<b>Think about this.</b>

152
00:12:37.958 --> 00:12:43.208
<b>As the desire,  so the result.</b>

153
00:12:43.208 --> 00:12:46.291


